# Tester / release (minimal)

Authoritative detail: `release/testers/README.txt`. Packaging script: `android/scripts/make-tester-release.ps1`.

## Build policy

- Do **not** produce tester APK/AAB automatically after feature or bug work
- Build tester APK only after an **explicit** user request (preferably after release analysis)
- `tNNN` (distribution sequence) and `versionCode` are **separate** concepts; never reuse either casually

## Artifacts

- Telegram APK comes **only** from `release/testers/CURRENT/`
- `archive/` is immutable — do not overwrite past entries
- Build event ≠ distribution/send — never invent `DISTRIBUTION_LOG` facts
- Do not send Gradle `app-production-release.apk`, debug, accelerated, or androidTest APKs as tester builds

## Updates

Data-preserving update: same package + same release cert + valid higher `versionCode` path. Never uninstall a tester’s production app as a convenience workaround.

## Volatile — do not hardcode in rules

Current `tNNN`, `versionCode`, APK hash, HEAD → read `release/testers/CURRENT/BUILD_INFO.txt` and/or `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`.
